      "message": "feels like we can extract just this part: pop_flog() vs pop_flog_dt() and keep the rest of the loop unchanged.\n\nso, something like this?\n```\nstruct parsed_flog_entry {\n  bool end_of_list;\n  char payload[MAX_PAYLOAD_SIZE];\n  size_t payload_size;\n  uint64_t raw_timestamp; // 32 bits for cr50 fit in 64 bits\n  time_t timestamp;\n  uintXX_t event_type; // cr50 8-bit (iirc) entry type should fit\n}\nwhile (retries--) {\n  parsed_flog_entry entry;\n  if (dt) { rv \u003d pop_flog_dt(\u0026entry) } else { rv \u003d pop_flog(\u0026entry) }\n  if (rv ) { ... }\n  if (entry.end_of_list) { ... no more entries ... }\n  if  (show_machine_output) {\n    printf(\"%10lu:%02x\", entry.raw_timestamp, entry.event_type);\n  } else {\n     ... also common code here ...\n  } \n}\n```",
